  "id": "stimulus-control",
  "term": "stimulus control",
  "definition": "Stimulus control is the careful control and clear reporting of the study materials used in research so that factors that can influence responses are accounted for. In this context, poor stimulus control makes findings harder to compare and validate across studies.",
